# Phase 3: BART Summarization Fine-Tuning + LLM Integration

Fine-tune `facebook/bart-large-cnn` on lecture transcripts for technical summarization, using FLAN-T5 for pseudo-summary generation and post-processing enhancement. Integrates Phase 2 models (NER, Topic-Seg, SBERT) for entity-aware training.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **GPU Memory**: BART-large-cnn (~1.6GB) + FLAN-T5-base (~990MB) won't fit simultaneously in 4GB VRAM. The plan processes them sequentially — FLAN-T5 runs first (Step 1), then is unloaded before BART training (Step 3). **If using Colab (T4 16GB), both can run more comfortably.**

> [!WARNING]
> **Pseudo-summaries quality**: The entire BART fine-tuning depends on FLAN-T5-generated pseudo-summaries. Step 1 includes quality filtering (SBERT similarity + entity coverage), but you should manually review ~20 summaries before proceeding to Step 3. The script will save samples for inspection.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Timeline Decision**: The plan below is designed for ~7 working days. Steps 1-2 (data prep) take ~2 days, Step 3 (BART training) ~2 days, Steps 4-6 (eval + enhancement + integration) ~3 days. Let me know if priorities need adjusting.

